Yeah, applying a patch is a bit more complicated than that. You have to
download the source code for nethack, and then apply the patch. The
patch is basically a list of changes that need to be made to the
original nethack source code to add the desired feature(s). You'll see
lines that start with a "-" and some start with a "+": these are lines
that have been added or removed from the original nethack source code.

In any case, i've applied a few popular and useful patches to the
nethack source code and supplied the result here:

http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/msg/b486466422a6ac85

You aren't the only one that has asked for xyz feature, and it was a
good exercise for me to learn about patching nethack anyways.

Hope it works for you.

